## Designer-to-frontend UI parity (chat shell)
- When implementing or migrating chat UI from `apps/designer`, preserve the accepted structural contract in `docs/designer-chat-styling.md` unless a product decision explicitly changes it.
- Required column structure for chat shell:
  - Flexbox-first (`flex flex-col`) per column with `h-full min-h-0` on the column shell.
  - Fixed header/footer via `shrink-0` (empty footer allowed when there is no footer UI).
  - Scrollable body via `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`.
- Shell-level: fixed viewport height and no page scroll for the chat layout; scroll only inside column bodies (match designer `h-dvh` / `overflow-hidden` pattern on outer wrappers).
- Preserve column-level borders and in-column header/footer dividers as in the designer shell (see doc).
- Preserve subtle incoming/outgoing message visual distinction and fixed message composer behavior in chat column.
- If frontend intentionally diverges from designer styling contract, update `docs/designer-chat-styling.md` and `.cursor/rules` in the same PR and explain the rationale.
